From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:08:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] monkey: skip sys/syscall.h and gettid on QNX

mk_scheduler.c includes <sys/syscall.h> on every non-Windows system to get
__NR_gettid. The QNX SDP 8.0 has no <sys/syscall.h> and no gettid syscall.

Skip the include on QNX and use pthread_self() for the worker label stored
in worker->pid. QNX thread ids are per process, which is enough: the value
only names the worker in logs.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 lib/monkey/mk_server/mk_scheduler.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/monkey/mk_server/mk_scheduler.c b/lib/monkey/mk_server/mk_scheduler.c
index f359b6f..d7b2b8a 100644
--- a/lib/monkey/mk_server/mk_scheduler.c
+++ b/lib/monkey/mk_server/mk_scheduler.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 
 #include <signal.h>
 
-#ifndef _WIN32
+#if !defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__QNXNTO__)
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -291,6 +291,8 @@ static int mk_sched_register_thread(struct mk_server *server)
     uint64_t tid;
     pthread_threadid_np(NULL, &tid);
     worker->pid = tid;
+#elif defined(__QNXNTO__)
+    worker->pid = (pid_t) pthread_self(); /* QNX tids are per-process */
 #else
     worker->pid = 0xdeadbeef;
 #endif
